  "problem": "The function $f(x,y)$ is defined as \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{y}^{3}-x+2.\n$$\n\nEvaluate this function at the point $(5,-1).$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(5,-1),$ we substitute $x=5$ and $y=-1$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5,-1) & =(3{y}^{3}-x+2){|}_{(5,-1)} \\\\  & =3(-1)^{3}-5+2 \\\\  & =-3-5+2 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
